## 3. YAML Spec Schema — Fields That Define an Agent

Based on `AgentSpec` (Pydantic model in `src/consilium/agentspec.py`) and the actual YAML files:

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| **`version`** | `str` (top-level) | Yes (`default: "1"`) | Spec version — only `"1"` is supported |
| **`agent.extend`** | `str` \| `null` | No | Path to another agent YAML to extend (relative to this file's directory). Special value `"default"` resolves to `agents/default/agent.yaml`. If absent, the spec is a root/base. |
| **`agent.name`** | `str` | Yes (unless inherited) | Display/identifier name for the agent |
| **`agent.system_prompt_path`** | `str` (path) | Yes (unless inherited) | Path to system prompt `.md` file. Currently all point to `system.md` which triggers assembled-prompt mode. |
| **`agent.system_prompt_args`** | `dict[str, str]` | No (default: `{}`) | Static string arguments substituted into the system prompt via `${PLACEHOLDER}` syntax. Merged with parent during inheritance. |
| **`agent.system_prompt_args_files`** | `dict[str, str]` (paths) | No (default: `{}`) | Like `system_prompt_args` but values are file paths whose contents are read at load time. File wins over inline if both specify the same key. |
| **`agent.model`** | `str` \| `null` | No | Default model alias. Overrides parent. |
| **`agent.when_to_use`** | `str` \| `null` | No | Inline usage guidance text. Overrides parent. |
| **`agent.when_to_use_file`** | `str` (path) \| `null` | No | File path to load `when_to_use` from. File wins over inline. |
| **`agent.tools`** | `list[str]` \| `null` | Yes (unless inherited) | **Full replacement** of the tool list from the parent. Each string is a Python import path like `"module:ClassName"`. |
| **`agent.allowed_tools`** | `list[str]` \| `null` | No | **Whitelist** filter applied on top of inherited tools. If set, only tools in this list are kept. Resolved to `None` (no filter) if inherited but not explicitly set. |
| **`agent.exclude_tools`** | `list[str]` \| `null` | No | **Blacklist** — tools to remove from the inherited+whitelisted set. Resolved to `[]` if inherited but not explicitly set. |
| **`agent.subagents`** | `dict[str, SubagentSpec]` | No (default: `{}`) | Map of subagent type name → `{path: <yaml path>, description: <text>}`. Overrides parent entirely (not merged). Set empty to prevent recursive registration. |
| **`agent.min_summary_length`** | `int` \| `null` | No | Minimum summary length in characters. `0` disables continuation prompting. |

### Tool Resolution Logic (from `_load_agent_spec`)

When extending, tools are resolved in this order:

1. **Start** with parent's `tools` list (or base if no parent)
2. If child specifies `tools` (not Inherit) → **replace** parent's tool list entirely
3. If child specifies `allowed_tools` (not Inherit) → **intersect** current tool list with `allowed_tools`
4. If child specifies `exclude_tools` (not Inherit) → **subtract** `exclude_tools` from current tool list

```python
# Simplified logic:
base_agent_spec.tools = agent_spec.tools           # replace (if not inherit)
if allowed: base_agent_spec.tools = intersect(...)  # whitelist
if excluded: base_agent_spec.tools = minus(...)     # blacklist
```

### Subagent Registration Schema (`SubagentSpec`)

Each entry in `subagents` is an object with:
- **`path`**: Path to the subagent's YAML file (resolved relative to parent YAML's directory)
- **`description`**: Text description used when the parent agent decides which subagent to call

### System Prompt Assembly

The `system.md` files contain only `<!-- assembled-from-sections -->`. When the loader (`_load_system_prompt` in `soul/agent.py`) sees this marker, it calls `assemble_system_prompt()` from `prompts/system/__init__.py`, which reads all 8 `.md` files from `src/consilium/prompts/system/`:
- `identity.md`, `coding_guidelines.md`, `prompt_and_tool_use.md`, `research_guidelines.md`, `working_environment.md`, `project_info.md`, `skills.md`, `ultimate_reminders.md`

The `ROLE_ADDITIONAL` system_prompt_arg is then injected into the assembled prompt (typically at the end of the identity section or appended). This is the mechanism that customizes the generic assembled prompt per subagent type.[stage] run_soul_finished

